=========================================================================
1. CONTRAST — text-red-400 (#f87171) on the header's ACTUAL background
=========================================================================

Correction to the dispatch's own arithmetic: /lead-dev's code comment in
SettingsForm.tsx computes text-red-400 against `#1a1f1a` (tailwind.config.ts
`colors.background`) and gets ~6:1. That token is the PUBLIC (website) route
group's background, not the admin shell's. Traced the actual paint order for
the admin dashboard instead:

  src/app/admin/layout.tsx            -> passthrough, no bg class at all
  src/app/admin/(dashboard)/layout.tsx:39
      <div className="flex min-h-screen bg-[#0a0a0a]">   <- opaque, full-bleed
        <aside className="... bg-black ...">              (sidebar only)
        <main className="min-w-0 flex-grow">               <- NO bg class
          <div className="p-8 md:p-12">{children}</div>    <- NO bg class

SettingsHeader is the first child rendered inside that unstyled <main>/<div>
stack in all six client files (confirmed by grep — no wrapping SettingsCard,
no bg-* class between the header and the dashboard's outer div). So the
color actually behind the header's text is `#0a0a0a` (tailwind.config.ts
`colors.surface`), not `#1a1f1a`.

WCAG relative-luminance contrast, computed by hand (sRGB -> linear -> L,
then (L1+0.05)/(L2+0.05)):

  text-red-400 #f87171  -> L = 0.32962
  bg  #0a0a0a  (surface) -> L = 0.00304   (actual, confirmed background)
  bg  #1a1f1a  (background, public site token — NOT what renders here)
                          -> L = 0.01275

  Contrast on #0a0a0a (actual): (0.32962+0.05)/(0.00304+0.05) ≈ 7.16:1
  Contrast on #1a1f1a (for reference only, not the real bg): ≈ 6.05:1
    (this second number matches /lead-dev's own comment almost exactly,
    confirming the arithmetic itself was right — only the background
    swatch it was checked against was wrong)

Both numbers clear WCAG AA (4.5:1 for normal text; text-sm/14px + normal
weight here is not "large text", so the 4.5:1 bar applies, not 3:1) with
comfortable margin. The real, applicable number (7.16:1) also clears AAA
(7:1) for normal text, by a hair. VERDICT: PASS, and better than claimed.

Icon (TriangleAlert, size=15) carries no color class of its own — it
inherits `currentColor` from the parent <p className="... text-red-400">,
exactly like ImageUploadField.tsx's existing error icon. Same 7.16:1 figure
applies to the icon's stroke.

