4. LONG MESSAGES / NARROW WIDTHS (item 3 of the dispatch)
=========================================================================

Static, logged-out repro (repro-source.html, compiled with this project's
actual tailwind.config.ts color tokens via `npx tailwindcss`, then shot with
headless Chrome via CDP — same tool this project already used for public-
page /qa live screenshots, no new dependency added) at 360 / 768 / 1024px:

  01-error-header-mobile-360.png   — delete-guard-shaped message (4 joined
                                      category names in quotes) and the
                                      ContactSettingsClient "·"-joined
                                      two-failure message both wrap cleanly
                                      across multiple lines; no horizontal
                                      overflow, no clipped text, no scrollbar.
  02-error-header-tablet-768.png   — same, more headroom, same result.
  03-error-header-desktop-1024.png — same messages stay on one line at this
                                      width; still no overflow.

No `truncate`/`whitespace-nowrap`/fixed-width ancestor sits between the
error <p> and the viewport edge — the flex row (icon `flex-none` + text)
wraps at normal word boundaries. This holds regardless of message length,
so it doesn't depend on the specific sample strings used above; those were
chosen to be at-or-beyond the longest plausible real message (all-8-category
delete-guard names would be more extreme still, but the wrap mechanism is
length-independent — no code path here special-cases the two samples shown).

Pre-existing, out of T-012's diff, NOT fixed here (flagged only): at 360px
the header's own title/button row (`flex items-start justify-between`,
unchanged by this diff) wraps "Contact & General Settings" to 3 lines and
"Save Changes" to 2 — visible in 01-error-header-mobile-360.png, case 3.
Byte-identical class list before/after T-012's diff; not a regression this
ticket introduced, not in this ticket's file scope to fix.

=========================================================================
5. MOTION (item 4 of the dispatch)
=========================================================================

No animation/transition class was added to the error <p> or its parent
<header> — confirmed by reading the diff (git diff -- SettingsForm.tsx):
zero new `transition-*`/`animate-*`/`duration-*` utilities. This matches
ImageUploadField.tsx's own error/warning blocks, which also mount with no
transition. Deliberately kept that way here rather than adding one: the
dispatch's own item 1 asks whether this is "one error language" — adding
motion to only the header's version while the field-level sibling has none
would itself be a new inconsistency. No prefers-reduced-motion guard was
needed because no motion was added.

